5,1,1,talk,Midori,,I think it's important we understand where our previous gaps were. I'd like to look into support ownership during last winter's outage and warehouse rule changes after new accounts.,"{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,"I'll focus on the operational side. I want to see the depot calendar and the peak-season cutover, as well as the yard devices and the 2021 scheduling trial.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,May,,I'll take a look at the upgrade history of the dispatch tool and the data lift in the 2018 pay move. I want to see how things actually hold up over time.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Misaki,,"I'll look into administrator retirements and hiring times, and the depot supervisors and the last rollout. I'm concerned about our capacity to handle the transition.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,"To ensure we aren't surprised by the long-term financial commitments, I'll examine the board minutes on capital and operating requests and the five years of renewal invoices.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Midori,,"Does anyone else feel we should double-check the human element? @Misaki, your choices seem very prudent given our current staffing levels.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"I agree with Midori. While the hardware is a priority, the human factor is a variable we cannot ignore. I will stick with my choices for now.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,May,,"I'm curious if we're missing something about the actual costs, but @Benjamin has that covered. I'll stay with my focus on the technical debt and external hand-offs.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Misaki,,"Thank you, Midori. I believe the gap between the official plan and the reality on the ground is where most risks hide, so I'll keep my focus there.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,It seems we have a comprehensive spread. I'm quite content to let the numbers tell their story while the rest of you investigate the operational friction.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Midori,,I think we've covered all the bases quite well. I'm happy to proceed with these selections if everyone is satisfied.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I am satisfied. The distribution of research covers the financial, technical, and operational risks effectively.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,May,,I'm satisfied too. Let's see what the records actually reveal about our habits.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Misaki,,I am also satisfied. I look forward to seeing how our findings align.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. It is a rare pleasure to have such a harmonious start to a procurement process. I believe we are ready to move forward.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
