35,2,1,talk,Midori,,It seems my suspicions were correct. We have a serious issue with accountability during outages and a tendency for our project scopes to become obsolete almost immediately.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"My findings confirm that our physical environment is a major hurdle. The peak-season schedule is unforgiving, and our current yard hardware is far too outdated for generic tools to work.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,May,,"I've found that we have a habit of letting systems rot in place because we can't find the time to upgrade them, and our reliance on external data migration has left us with lingering errors.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"The staffing situation is precarious. We are losing key institutional knowledge through retirements, and the training from previous rollouts didn't actually stick with the depot supervisors.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Interestingly, the board seems to have a blind spot for recurring operating costs while trimming capital requests, and our renewal invoices show that fragmented licensing leads to steady price creep.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Benjamin, that price creep sounds dangerous. If we choose a modular system, are we just signing up for more of those climbing costs you mentioned?","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"That is a valid concern. If the system is too fragmented, it may also fail to survive the rigid constraints of our peak-season calendar and the reality of our yard hardware.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,May,,"Exactly. If we go for something that requires constant updates or external specialists for every tweak, we're just repeating the cycle of technical debt and messy data lifts.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"And if the implementation is too complex, our remaining administrators won't be able to support it, and the depot supervisors will simply ignore the new processes again.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"Precisely. We need a solution that avoids the ""death by a thousand cuts"" in the budget, while remaining simple enough that it doesn't require a small army of consultants to keep it breathing.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Midori,,It sounds like we all agree that stability and clear ownership are paramount. We cannot afford another situation where no one is in charge when things break.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,We must prioritize a vendor that can handle the physical reality of our depots without requiring a total overhaul of our hardware or a miracle in our scheduling.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,May,,"I'm leaning toward something that doesn't rely on a partner firm for the heavy lifting, as those external hand-offs seem to be where our data quality goes to die.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Misaki,,"I agree. We need a vendor that provides direct, hands-on support during the rollout to ensure the depot supervisors actually adopt the system this time.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"I concur. A vendor that bundles its services and provides a clear, predictable cost structure would be far more palatable than a collection of independent licenses.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Midori,,"I think we've identified our non-negotiables: clear accountability, operational resilience, and a sustainable cost model. I'm ready to see which candidates actually fit these needs.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,I agree. We have a clear set of criteria now. I am ready to evaluate the candidates against these operational and financial realities.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,May,,I'm ready as well. Let's hope the candidates offer more than just polished sales pitches and a list of features we can't actually maintain.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"I am also ready. I hope we find a partner who understands that the success of this system depends on the people using it, not just the software itself.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,I believe we have reached a consensus on our priorities. Let us see which of these vendors possesses the fortitude to survive our environment and the transparency to satisfy our budget.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
55,2,4,pass,Benjamin,,Over,"{""forced"":false,""empty"":false,""trailing"":true}"
