61,3,1,talk,Midori,,"Looking at the options, Meridian Systems seems strong with its fixed configuration and regional support, which could solve our accountability and scope issues.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Anchor Industrial Software is the most compelling for me; having an engineering team present through rollout is the only way to ensure it survives our yards and calendar.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,May,,I'm wary of Tessera because of that partner firm handling migration; we've already seen how external data lifts can leave us with a year of errors.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Misaki,,"I agree with May. Anchor's on-site engineering team seems far more reliable for our supervisors than a partner firm, and it addresses our staffing shortages directly.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Corvus is a non-starter for me; modular components and independent licensing are exactly the recipe for the price creep and budget fragmentation I discovered.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Ryuji, Anchor's on-site presence is appealing, but does their on-premise server model create a new accountability gap if the hardware fails, or is that handled by their team?","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Given their engineering team is present through rollout, I suspect they take more ownership of the environment than a hosted provider would, which aligns with our need for stability.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,May,,"I'm still leaning toward Anchor as well. Meridian's ""fixed configuration"" sounds like it might clash with the warehouse rule changes Midori found, whereas Anchor's engineers can adapt on the fly.","{""words"":30,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"I agree with May. Anchor's approach seems the most realistic for our depot supervisors, as having engineers on-site is far more effective than a manual or a remote trainer.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"While on-premise servers require a capital outlay, it avoids the recurring subscription creep of Tessera and the fragmented billing of Corvus. Anchor seems the most fiscally transparent and operationally robust choice.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm convinced. Anchor's on-site engineering team provides the accountability we've been missing, and it seems to be the only option that truly respects the reality of our operations.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,"I am in full agreement. Anchor is the only candidate that addresses the physical and scheduling constraints of our depots with a practical, hands-on deployment strategy.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,May,,"I'm sold on Anchor. It avoids the risks of external partners and the stagnation of fixed configurations, giving us the best chance at a clean, lasting implementation.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I agree completely. Anchor is the only choice that prioritizes the people and the actual environment over a theoretical plan.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"It is rare to find a solution that satisfies both the ledger and the loading dock, but Anchor appears to be that rare find. I am in agreement.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Midori,,I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,May,,I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
80,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for Anchor Industrial Software.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
